From 05fae217c05f5234ac2de69f5901634aecfa8084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Feb 2026 16:56:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Multi-destination trip form and dashboard spending insights

### Motivation

- Allow trips to contain multiple destinations and improve the create/edit UX so users can add/remove stops without external APIs.
- Normalize and persist multi-stop data safely so the first stop becomes the primary destination when a primary is not provided.
- Provide useful spending insights on the dashboard (total expenses, budgets, savings, highest/lowest spend) to help users manage trip costs.

### Description

- Added `TripFormViewModel` and `TripDestinationInput` in `ViewModels/TripFormViewModel.cs` and switched trip create/edit flows to use this view model.
- Updated `TripsController` to accept the view model, populated trip objects from the form via `BuildDestinations`, and added helpers `NormalizePrimaryDestination` and `EnsureDestinationRow` to keep `ModelState` valid and support multiple destinations.
- Reworked create/edit views (`Views/Trips/Create.cshtml`, `Views/Trips/Edit.cshtml`) to render a dynamic destinations table with client-side JS to add/remove rows and to bind `Destinations[index].City`/`Nights`.
- Updated trip details (`Views/Trips/Details.cshtml`) to display stops and driving distance, and refined the trips list filter label to use `current` (controller logic already supports it).
- Replaced/rewrote the dashboard controller to `DashboardController` and introduced `DashboardViewModel` (`ViewModels/DashboardViewModel.cs`) to compute per-trip spend summaries, total budget, and estimated savings; updated `Views/Dashboard/Index.cshtml` to present these insights.

### Testing

- No automated tests were run because the `dotnet` SDK was not available in the environment so `dotnet build`/test could not be executed.
